  "result": "Excellent! All 142 tests pass. I've added comprehensive date utilities in UTC:\n\n**`src/dates.js` \u2014 Three UTC-based date functions:**\n\n**`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Checks format matches /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/\n- Verifies the date actually exists (e.g., rejects Feb 30)\n- Uses UTC to avoid timezone issues\n- Returns: `true` or `false`\n\n**`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds days to a date string\n- Works in UTC (no timezone confusion)\n- Handles negative numbers for subtraction\n- Crosses month/year boundaries correctly\n- Handles leap years\n- Example: `addDays('2026-10-07', 5)` \u2192 `'2026-10-12'`\n- Example: `addDays('2024-02-28', 1)` \u2192 `'2024-02-29'` (leap year)\n\n**`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Calculates days from date a to date b\n- Returns integer number of whole days\n- Works in UTC\n- Negative if b < a\n- Example: `daysBetween('2026-10-07', '2026-10-12')` \u2192 `5`\n- Example: `daysBetween('2026-10-12', '2026-10-07')` \u2192 `-5`\n\n**Updated `createInvoice`** \u2014 Now uses `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed local duplicate function\n- Uses UTC-based validation\n\n**Test coverage:** 37 new tests covering:\n- Format validation (valid/invalid formats)\n- Non-existent dates (Feb 30, Apr 31, etc.)\n- Leap years (Feb 29)\n- Adding/subtracting days\n- Month/year boundaries\n- Large time spans\n- Inverse relationship between addDays and daysBetween\n\n**Key guarantee:** All date operations use UTC exclusively, so dates never depend on the machine's local timezone. `'2026-10-07'` means the same thing everywhere.\n\nAll 142 tests pass \u2713",
